            "text": "In the Hong Kong Chinese Orchestra, the wind instruments in use include the bangdi, qudi, dadi andxindi; soprano keyed sheng, alto paisheng and bass baosheng; the alto guan, bass guan and suona, etc.. Depending on the repertory, the Orchestra also incorporates other wind instruments such as the dongxiao, bawu, xun, koudi and conch. Contact Us Copyright © 2026 HKCO View Desktop Version Your Support The HKCO is a non-profit organization. It is through your support that we can continue to make life beautiful, with arts, music, and a thankful heart. Sponsorship & Donation Advertisement Subscribe Newsletter Sign up for emails about special offers, discounts, latest news, and more. Go Please enter a valid email. Friends of HKCO Download Application Form Contact Us Copyright © 2026 HKCO View Mobile Version //Google Analytic (function(i,s,o,g,r,a,m){i['GoogleAnalyticsObject']=r;i[r]=i[r]||function(){ (i[r].q=i[r].q||[]).push(arguments)},i[r].l=1*new Date();a=s.createElement(o), m=s.getElementsByTagName(o)[0];a.async=1;a.src=g;m.parentNode.insertBefore(a,m) })(window,document,'script','https://www.google-analytics.com/analytics.js','ga'); ga('create', 'UA-76405764-1', 'auto'); ga('send', 'pageview');\n"
